# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This file is the only thing standing between a personal database and a public
# repository, so it is deliberately over-broad and self-contained.
#
# Self-contained matters: several of these were previously covered only by
# Blake's *global* gitignore (~/.config/git/ignore), which does not travel with
# a clone. On any other machine — or a CI checkout — they would have been
# committed. Rules that protect secrets belong in the repo, not in a profile.
#
# `npm run publish-check` verifies the intent behind this file rather than its
# text: it asks git whether the sensitive paths are actually ignored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

node_modules/
dist/
build/
out/
*.log

# ---- The database, in every form it takes -------------------------------
# `data/` at any depth, not just the root: packages/server/data/ is where the
# real one lives.
data/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
# WAL/shared-memory sidecars, and hand-made backups like everything.db.bak-1115
# — a bare *.db would not catch those.
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db.*
*.sqlite.*

# ---- Secrets -------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets/
*.vault

# Holds this machine's bearer token.
agent.config.json
# The feature switches are a local deployment choice, not a project fact.
# features.json is per-install; features.example.json is the checked-in one.
features.json

# ---- Personal artefacts --------------------------------------------------
# The overlay avatar and the app logo are Blake's own pictures, written beside
# the database. `data/` already covers them; named too, so moving the folder
# cannot silently start committing them.
avatar.*
logo.png
logo.jpg
logo.gif
logo.webp
!packages/web/public/avatar-placeholder.*

# Runtime logs from scripts/start.ps1 (46MB and counting, full of window titles
# — which is to say, a log of everything he has had open).
logs/

# ---- Large third-party binaries -----------------------------------------
# Voice models: ~150MB of third-party binaries, downloaded by voice-setup.
# Not ours, not small, and not something a git history should carry.
#
# They live inside the voice feature so that deleting the feature reclaims the
# disk. Matched by folder name at any depth as well as by the exact path — this
# rule named the pre-move location for a while, and an ignore rule that silently
# stops matching is how 150MB of binaries end up in a first public commit.
packages/agent/src/features/voice/models/
**/features/voice/models/
packages/agent/models/

# ---- Editor and tooling --------------------------------------------------
# Was only ever ignored globally. It records local permission grants and
# absolute paths from this machine.
.claude/settings.local.json
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
